    "4.3",
    "System file used by Microsoft Windows NT and later for the system boot process; contains settings and scripts that load resources for the operating system; must not be modified, moved, or deleted or the computer may not be able to start up. Example NT files include CONFIG.NT and AUTOEXEC.NT. Windows Microsoft Windows. File used by theWord free Bible software; contains a copy of the New Testament and uses a plain text format; includes embedded tags that are interpreted by theWord when displaying the chapter and verse structure; used for distributing digital copies of the New Testament. Usually NT files are downloaded as .nt.exe executables that self-install the copy of the New Testament when opened. Windows theWordFree.",
